<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H20053</pnldref><english><title>Enters / remains in a designated area overseas - terrorism</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>Counter terrorism</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>terror</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>terrorist</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>terrorism</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>border</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>security</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>enter</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>enters</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>entering</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>entered</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>remain</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>remains</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>remained</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>remaining</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>United Kingdom</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>UK</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>national</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>resident</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>designated area</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>designated</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>area</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>designated areas</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>areas</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>Counter Terrorism and Border Security Act 2019</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..), being a United Kingdom national or United Kingdom resident, without reasonable excuse&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;(A)_[entered]&lt;br /&gt;(B)_[remained in]&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;a designated area, namely **(..SPECIFY DETAILS..)</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to section 58B(1) and (9) of the Terrorism Act 2000.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt;being a United Kingdom national / resident&lt;br /&gt;entered / remained&lt;br /&gt;in a designated area overseas</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>(i) The consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Attorney General is required, see section 117 of the Terrorism Act 2000.&lt;br /&gt;(ii) As per section 58B(2), it is a defence for a person charged with an offence under this section to prove that the person had a reasonable excuse for entering, or remaining in, the designated area.&lt;br /&gt;(iii) See sections 58B(3) and (4) for exceptions to this offence.&lt;br /&gt;(iv) Terrorism is defined in section 1 of the Terrorism Act 2000.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code